WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.347
Where the force goes.

2
00:00:01.507 --> 00:00:07.776
Every model has parts that carry weight: the legs of a figure, the bottom of a tower, the neck under a heavy head.

3
00:00:07.936 --> 00:00:12.301
Those parts are under stress, and they are the parts you build strongest.

4
00:00:13.001 --> 00:00:14.348
Shape is strength.

5
00:00:14.508 --> 00:00:17.295
The same card is weak flat and strong folded.

6
00:00:17.455 --> 00:00:18.987
A tube carries weight.

7
00:00:19.147 --> 00:00:21.098
A triangle cannot squash out of shape.

8
00:00:21.258 --> 00:00:23.951
Before you reach for more tape, change the shape.

9
00:00:24.651 --> 00:00:26.137
The skeleton first.

10
00:00:26.297 --> 00:00:28.759
An armature is the wire skeleton inside.

11
00:00:28.919 --> 00:00:31.891
Bend it into the pose, then build the body around it.

12
00:00:32.051 --> 00:00:35.766
A thin arm held out in the air needs wire inside, or it flops.

13
00:00:36.466 --> 00:00:37.952
A diary of the build.

14
00:00:38.112 --> 00:00:45.171
Photograph the skeleton before the body hides it, and each stage as you go, with a note of what you changed and why.

15
00:00:45.331 --> 00:00:49.789
Read it before the next model, and last time's fix becomes this time's plan.
